      "Language": "eng",
      "Abstract": {"AbstractText": [
        {
          "NlmCategory": "BACKGROUND",
          "Label": "IMPORTANCE OF THE FIELD",
          "content": "Coronary artery disease remains the leading cause of mortality in the industrialized world. Despite advances in surgical and catheter-based interventions, a select number of patients remain with no options for invasive therapy. The goal of this review is to discuss the current status of pharmacotherapeutic interventions to treat end-stage coronary artery disease."
        },
        {
          "NlmCategory": "METHODS",
          "Label": "AREAS COVERED IN THIS REVIEW",
          "content": "Literature review on the topic of therapeutic angiogenesis from 1980 to 2009."
        },
        {
          "NlmCategory": "RESULTS",
          "Label": "WHAT THE READER WILL GAIN",
          "content": "Insight into current therapeutic strategies employed to manage end-stage coronary artery disease."
        },
        {
          "NlmCategory": "CONCLUSIONS",
          "Label": "TAKE HOME MESSAGE",
          "content": "A promising approach focuses on augmenting the endogenous angiogenic response to chronic myocardial ischemia via the use of growth factors."
        }
      ]},
